        "mollifier_fderiv: both actual C-infinity compact convolution and actual convolution of Frechet derivative; positive canonical Haar normalized kernel, no derivative certificate.",
        "mollifier_squared_error: continuity, global boundedness, positive mass-one convolution bound, pointwise convergence at every x, finite-measure dominated convergence for squared errors.",
        "compact_c1_approximation: compact f and derivative bounded and continuous; same sequence approximates both. No common-support or uniform-convergence premise needed.",
        "l2_convergence: actual quotient inner product/norm-square integral, AE representatives, square-root continuity.",
        "Public proof derives real gradient compactness/continuity through Riesz isometry, both MemLp facts and same closed graph membership from simultaneous L2 convergence."
      ],
